P8-fips-001 patch (outside its write_scope): README.md, SECURITY_CLAIMS.md, compliance/COMPLIANCE_MAP.md.

Rationale: PREFLIGHT-8 D-P8.1 and the `fips-boundary` oracle "cert #5298 cited for the static build -> red" make
`python3 -I ci/fips-boundary.py` fail on three existing lines that cite "#5298/#5314" (or "#5298 and #5314") for
the cmvp build. aws-lc-fips-sys =0.13.11 builds AWS-LC FIPS 3.1.0 statically by default on Linux, so the cmvp build
is the static module, CMVP #5314 (policy 140sp5314.pdf v1.2, sha256 pinned in compliance/fips-boundary.toml);
#5298 is the dynamic module and applies only to a dynamic build. This patch rewrites only those three citations so
each names #5314 for the static build and says #5298 is dynamic; it makes no other claim change and adds no 0x11ED
claim text (that is P8-compliance-001's D-P8.1 wording). SECURITY_CLAIMS.md and compliance/** are in
P8-compliance-001's write_scope; README.md is in no Phase-8 unit's scope, so the integrator applies it. With the patch
applied, fips-boundary, tcb-lines and compliance check were run on a scratch copy (see the unit's final report).
Apply with: git apply units/phase-8/patches/P8-fips-001.patch

